{"reply":"You have ₱9,050.00 a month not yet allocated from ₱100,000.00 income, ₱76,000.00 spending, and ₱14,950.00 minimum debt payments. Right now the credit card is first in your avalanche order, and the emergency fund covers 2.1 months against your 3-month target.

So this is really a trade-off between Mara’s wish to clear the card fast and Jun’s wish to keep building cash. The card is expensive at 3% a month, but your approved choice last session was a bigger cash buffer over paying debt faster. I would weigh how comfortable you feel staying below the 3-month emergency target while you attack the card.

